{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.\n\nSummary:\n1. Primary Request and Intent:\n   The user (via the cobbler orchestrator) assigned task #5236: implement `cmd/readlink` for the go-unix-utils project, specifically requirements R1.1 through R1.4 from srd050-readlink. This is a stitch task in a code generation pipeline. The task requires creating two files: `cmd/readlink/main.go` (the readlink utility) and `cmd/readlink/readlink_test.go` (differential tests against greadlink). The implementation must match GNU greadlink behavior byte-for-byte on stdout and exit code. No git commands should be run; git is managed externally.\n\n2. Key Technical Concepts:\n   - Differential testing pattern: compare Go binary output against GNU reference binary (greadlink)\n   - SIGPIPE handling via `sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler()`\n   - `os.Readlink()` for reading symlink targets\n   - `filepath.EvalSymlinks()` or manual canonicalization for -f and -e modes\n   - `pkg/testutils.BuildBinary(t, \".\")` for compiling test binaries\n   - `pkg/testutils.RunDiffTests()` for running differential test cases\n   - `exec.LookPath(\"greadlink\")` with `t.Skip` for graceful test skipping\n   - LC_ALL=C environment for all tests\n   - Go module: `github.com/petar-djukic/go-unix-utils`\n   - Function size limit: 40 lines max (E8)\n   - File size limit: 500 lines max (E9)\n   - Copyright header required: `// Copyright (c) 2026 Petar Djukic. All rights reserved.` + `// SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT`\n\n3. Files and Code Sections:\n   - **docs/specs/software-requirements/srd050-readlink.yaml** (read to understand requirements)\n     - R1.1: When invoked with a symlink operand and no flags, print immediate target + newline, exit 0\n     - R1.2: If operand is not a symbolic link (no flags), print nothing to stdout, exit 1\n     - R1.3: `-f` (`--canonicalize`) resolves full canonical path. Final component need not exist, but directory containing it must exist.\n     - R1.4: `-e` (`--canonicalize-existing`) resolves full canonical path. Every component must exist; otherwise exit 1.\n     - R1.5: `-m` (`--canonicalize-missing`) resolves full canonical path. No component need exist. (NOT in scope for this task)\n     - R1.6: `-n` (`--no-newline`) suppresses trailing newline for single operand. (NOT in scope)\n     - R2.1-R2.2: Multiple operands handling (NOT in scope)\n     - R3.1: No operand → usage error to stderr, exit 1\n     - R3.2: Unknown flags → error to stderr, exit 1\n     - non_goals: No --relative-to or --relative-base (use realpath instead)\n   \n   - **pkg/sys/sigpipe.go** (read for SIGPIPE handler pattern)\n     ```go\n     // Copyright (c) 2026 Petar Djukic. All rights reserved.\n     // SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT\n     package sys\n     import (\n         \"os\"\n         \"os/signal\"\n         \"syscall\"\n     )\n     func InstallSIGPIPEHandler() {\n         c := make(chan os.Signal, 1)\n         signal.Notify(c, syscall.SIGPIPE)\n         go func() {\n             <-c\n             os.Exit(0)\n         }()\n     }\n     ```\n\n   - **pkg/testutils/difftest.go** (provided inline in project_context)\n     - Key exports: `DiffTest` struct, `RunDiffTests()`, `BuildBinary()`, `NormalizeFunc`, `ComposeNormalizers()`, `TimestampNormalizer`\n     - `DiffTest` struct: `Name`, `Args`, `Stdin`, `Env`, `WorkDir`, `ExitCode`, `Normalize`, `ExpectedFiles`\n     - `RunDiffTests(t *testing.T, goBinary, refBinary string, tests []DiffTest)` runs each test case as a subtest\n     - `buildEnv()` merges test env with OS env and sets LC_ALL=C by default\n\n   - **pkg/testutils/build.go** (not read, but referenced - provides `BuildBinary(t, \".\")`)\n\n   - **cmd/readlink/main.go** - TO BE CREATED\n   - **cmd/readlink/readlink_test.go** - TO BE CREATED\n\n4. Errors and fixes:\n   - No errors encountered yet; implementation has not started.\n\n5. Problem Solving:\n   - Read the SRD to understand the four requirements (R1.1-R1.4) that need to be implemented\n   - Read the SIGPIPE handler to understand the calling pattern\n   - Reviewed the inline project_context for testutils patterns, shared protocols, and coding standards\n\n6. All user messages:\n   - Message 1: The massive task prompt containing the full project context, task description, execution constitution, coding standards, constraints, requirements, acceptance criteria, design decisions, shared protocols, and package contracts. This is the cobbler orchestrator's stitch task prompt for task #5236.\n\n7. Pending Tasks:\n   - Create `cmd/readlink/main.go` implementing R1.1-R1.4 (default readlink behavior, non-symlink handling, -f canonicalize, -e canonicalize-existing)\n   - Create `cmd/readlink/readlink_test.go` with differential tests against greadlink\n   - Run `go build -o bin/readlink ./cmd/readlink/` to verify compilation\n   - Run `go vet ./cmd/readlink/` to check for issues\n   - Run `go test ./cmd/readlink/... -count=1` to verify tests pass\n\n8. Current Work:\n   I had just finished reading the two required files (srd050-readlink.yaml and pkg/sys/sigpipe.go) and was about to begin implementing the readlink utility. I had gathered all the information needed:\n   - The SRD requirements R1.1-R1.4 to implement\n   - The SIGPIPE handler pattern to use\n   - The testutils API from the inline project_context\n   - The design decisions (D1-D5) and acceptance criteria (AC1-AC5)\n   \n   No code has been written yet. The implementation phase was about to begin.\n\n9. Optional Next Step:\n   Write both `cmd/readlink/main.go` and `cmd/readlink/readlink_test.go` in full, then compile and test. The implementation should:\n   \n   **main.go**: Parse flags (-f/--canonicalize, -e/--canonicalize-existing, plus -m and -n even though not in scope, to avoid unknown flag errors), call `sys.InstallSIGPIPE