r (--help, --version)\n   - Normalize binary names in error messages to match\n5. **Environment Setup**: Tests set `LC_ALL=C` in environment\n6. **Test Coverage**: \n   - Default behavior and explicit flags (-P, -L, --physical, --logical)\n   - Flag precedence and combinations (-LP, -PL, etc.)\n   - Error handling (unknown flags)\n   - Operand handling (extra args, args after --)\n   - Help and version output\n7. **Exit Code Testing**: Verifies exit codes (1 for errors, 0 for success)\n\nThe patterns show a well-structured utility with comprehensive differential testing against a reference implementation and proper error handling with appropriate exit codes."}]}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01b21283-8774-4233-ad4f-9374e7207806","uuid":"0edc2da0-5cdc-4c02-b252-d246084c7b12","timestamp":"2026-05-15T00:56:57.977Z","tool_use_result":{"status":"completed","prompt":"In the repo at /private/var/folders/dl/cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn/T/go-unix-utils-worktrees/5236, find an existing cmd/ utility that has both main.go and a _test.go file. I need to see the patterns used. Look at cmd/pwd/ since it was recently implemented (task 5235). Read both cmd/pwd/main.go and cmd/pwd/pwd_test.go in full. Also check if cmd/readlink/ directory exists already.","agentId":"ae8ca905d5f4baa83","agentType":"Explore","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Perfect! I have all the information you need. Here's my analysis:\n\n## Summary\n\n**cmd/readlink/ directory:** Does NOT exist yet - it needs to be created.\n\n**cmd/pwd/ structure:** Contains two files:\n- `main.go` (3,184 bytes)\n- `pwd_test.go` (2,853 bytes)\n\n## Key Patterns Found in cmd/pwd/\n\n### main.go Structure:\n1. **Header Comments**: Copyright notice and SPDX identifier, followed by a specification reference comment (srd051-pwd R1.1-R1.4, etc.)\n2. **Package declaration**: `package main`\n3. **Imports**: Standard library imports (fmt, os, path/filepath, strings) plus internal package (`github.com/petar-djukic/go-unix-uti